[Themes "d4-break,open-centre"]

1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O Nxe4 { Black grabs the pawn at once, accepting an open centre. }
6. d4 { Opens the centre while the black king is still in the middle. } 6... b5 7. Bb3 d5
8. dxe5 { Gains space and fixes a pawn on e5 that cramps Black's pieces. } 8... Be6
9. c3 { Supports d4 and gives the bishop on b3 a retreat, so the e5 pawn stays safe. } 9... Be7
10. Nbd2 { Challenges the strong black knight on e4. } 10... O-O
11. Bc2 { Aims the bishop at the knight on e4 and keeps it away from ...Na5 tricks. } 11... Bf5
12. Nb3 { Heads for d4 or c5 and eyes the loose pawn on b5 later. } *
